<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21012] The aarch64 testing is no longer using 64k page size</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21012</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The aarch64 testing is running with 4KiB PAGE_AIZE instead of the expected 64KiB size. This puts a big hole in the review and release testing for 2.18.0 and probably EXA7 as well. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This can be seen with clientarch=aarch64 sanity-sec 53 skips &lt;tt&gt;Need 64K PAGE_SIZE client&lt;/tt&gt; for 60-90 days (hard to search for when it started).  There is also sanity test_34h showing dd with 4096 byte writes instead of 65536 byte writes when &lt;tt&gt;$PAGE_SIZE&lt;/tt&gt; is used. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
